docstring:
Generates locations next to a cell that are a certain distance away

@param location The starting location from which others should be generated
@param radius The distance from the start locations should be retrieved from

function:
public List<Location> multLocationGeneration(Location location,Integer radius)
    {
        List<Location> locations = new LinkedList<Location>(); //Adjacent locations
        Integer minX = Math.max(location.getRow() - radius,0); //Furthest position from the animal to the left
        Integer maxX = Math.min(location.getRow() + radius,depth-1); //Furthest position from the animal to the right
        Integer minY = Math.max(location.getCol() - radius,0); //Furthest position from the animal going up
        Integer maxY = Math.min(location.getCol() + radius,width-1); //Furthest position from the animal going down
        for (int xPos = minX; xPos < maxX; xPos++) //For each x position...
        {
            int nextRow = xPos;
            for (int yPos = minY; yPos < maxY; yPos++){ //And for each y position...
                int nextCol = yPos;
                locations.add(new Location(nextRow, nextCol)); //Add the (x,y) to the list.
            }
        }
        return locations;
    }

