docstring:
Return a shuffled list of locations adjacent to the given one. The list will
not include the location itself. All locations will lie within the grid.

@param location
The location from which to generate adjacencies.
@param viewRadius
The radius of the square drawn around actor to look in. E.g. a
radius of 3 means look 3 blocks in all directions not including
the block the actor is standing on.
@return A list of locations adjacent to that given.

function:
public List<Location> adjacentLocations(Location location, int viewRadius) {
		assert location != null : "Null location passed to adjacentLocations";
		// The list of locations to be returned.
		List<Location> locations = new LinkedList<>();
		if (location != null) {
			int row = location.getRow();
			int col = location.getCol();
			for (int roffset = -viewRadius; roffset <= viewRadius; roffset++) {
				int nextRow = row + roffset;
				if (nextRow >= 0 && nextRow < depth) {
					for (int coffset = -viewRadius; coffset <= viewRadius; coffset++) {
						int nextCol = col + coffset;
						// Exclude invalid locations and the original location.
						if (nextCol >= 0 && nextCol < width && (roffset != 0 || coffset != 0)) {
							locations.add(new Location(nextRow, nextCol));
						}
					}
				}
			}

			// Shuffle the list. Several other methods rely on the list
			// being in a random order.
			Collections.shuffle(locations, rand);
		}
		return locations;
	}

