docstring:
Returns List of adjacent locations to parameter location
within the specified search radius
@param location The location used as reference
for the search
@param searchRadius The radius of the search
@return List of locations found in the search

function:
public List<Location> adjacentLocations(Location location, int searchRadius)
    {
        assert location != null : "Null location passed to adjacentLocations";
        // The list of locations to be returned.
        List<Location> locations = new LinkedList<>();
        if(location != null) {
            int row = location.getRow();
            int col = location.getCol();
            for(int roffset = -searchRadius; roffset <= searchRadius; roffset++) {
                int nextRow = row + roffset;
                if(nextRow >= 0 && nextRow < depth) {
                    for(int coffset = -searchRadius; coffset <= searchRadius; coffset++) {
                        int nextCol = col + coffset;
                        // Exclude invalid locations and the original location.
                        if(nextCol >= 0 && nextCol < width && (roffset != 0 || coffset != 0)) {
                            locations.add(new Location(nextRow, nextCol));
                        }//end of if column is valid
                    }//end of for all columns in search radius
                }//end of if row is valid
            }//end of for all rows in search radius

            // Shuffle the list. Several other methods rely on the list
            // being in a random order.
            Collections.shuffle(locations, rand);
        }
        return locations;
    }

