docstring:
Look for worms adjacent to the current location.
Only the first live worm is eaten.
@return Where food was found, or null if it wasn't.

function:
private Location findFood()
    {
        Field field = getField();
        List<Location> adjacent = field.adjacentLocations(getLocation(),1);
        Iterator<Location> it = adjacent.iterator();
        while(it.hasNext()) {
            Location where = it.next();
            Object animal = field.getObjectAt(where);
            if(animal instanceof Worm) {
                Worm worm = (Worm) animal;
                if(worm.isAlive()) { 
                    worm.setDead();
                    setFoodLevel(WORM_FOOD_VALUE);
                    return where;
                }
            }
        }
        return null;
    }

docstring:
Check whether or not this tiger is to give birth at this step.
New births will be made into free adjacent locations.
@param newtigers A list to return newly born tigers.

function:
private void giveBirth(List<Animal> newTigers)
    {
        Field field = getField();
        List<Location> adjacent = field.adjacentLocations(getLocation());
        Iterator<Location> it = adjacent.iterator();
        while(it.hasNext()) {
            Location where = it.next();
            Object animal = field.getObjectAt(where);
            if(animal instanceof Tiger) {
                Tiger tiger = (Tiger) animal;
                //Check if the gender of this tiger is opposite of the partner tiger. If is that the case, than the breeding is true.
                if(tiger.getGender() != this.getGender()) { 
                    List<Location> free = field.getFreeAdjacentLocations(getLocation());
                    int births = breed();
                    for(int b = 0; b < births && free.size() > 0; b++) {
                        Location loc = free.remove(0);
                        boolean genderSetter = setGender();
                        Tiger young = new Tiger(false, field, loc, genderSetter);
                        newTigers.add(young);
                    }
                }      
            }
        }
    }

